# Context

## Background
Review items 1 to 3 of the merged branch menubar-session-tags. The hub
authenticates a device by its credential, so the credential's Device ID
is the identity under which sessions and annotations are stored.

## Why This Way
- The rule "the credential names a paired device" already held for
  uploads; status, join, and mcp --remote now follow it instead of a
  second source of truth.
- A mismatch is reported, never repaired: ohya cannot know which file
  the owner wants to keep. The remedy names restore or delete.
- Join no longer creates device.json before it parses the code, so an
  invalid code leaves no identity behind (cli_test.go now proves --state
  by the created directory).

## Gotchas
- A state directory that both ohya ingest and ohya join use would need
  its device.json; the remedy text therefore says "delete it when only
  ohya join uses this state directory".
- No test covers the writer ID in the remote MCP tool description; the
  hub-side annotation writer is checked by serve_e2e_test.go.
